  <page_number>36</page_number>
  <running_head>I. IACOMOTI</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Hostisque dum fraudes recludit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Quae mala quósve tulit labores!</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Nulla rigenti frigore territum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Videre Bruma aut Andromedes Pater,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Et stella vesani Leonis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Cum segetes coquit æstus almas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Tantisque tandem mortibus addue,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Condæe Princeps, quo tua carmine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Dicenda, quo fletu riganda</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Fata truci properata fraude?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Non præliantem perdidit hosticus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">
      <i>Ensis duello, classica cum sonant,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Armata quando militantes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Per medias rapit ira cædes.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Sed tu occidisti progenies bona</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Magni parentis, Borbonicæ altera</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Spes gentis occultis veneni</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Insidiis superatus atri,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Quo delibutis muneribus ferox</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Medea quondam Colchica pellicem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Est ulta, quo parens superbis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Sævit imperiis Locusta.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Has prisca fraudes Gallia nesciens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">
      <i>Virtute sola &amp; Marte potentior</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Late per obstantes caternas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26" para="true">
      <i>Explicuit sua signa victrix.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Hinc sordidatis vestibus horridæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28" para="true">
      <i>Lugent Camœnæ, flent Charitum chori,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" para="true">
      <i>Et</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The fragment "Et" at the lower right is a line-start beginning the next stanza, set outside the text block; treated as a separate fragment. Long s rendered as s; italic throughout.</notes>
</page>
